NOTICE
======

This release bundles no third-party dataset, weight file, image record or
credential. The material below is either fetched by the user or referenced as a
dependency, and each entry keeps its own licence and source.

Public datasets
---------------

TotalSegmentator computed tomography dataset, release 2.0.1
  Licence : CC BY 4.0
  Source  : https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10047292
  Record  : "Dataset with segmentations of 117 important anatomical structures in
            1228 CT images", version 2.0.1, Zenodo record 10047292.
  Role    : abdominal vascular labels for pretraining the segmentation backbone.
  Note    : the concept DOI printed in the manuscript,
            https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6802613, resolves to the newest release
            of the same record family; the pinned version is the one above.
  Citation: Wasserthal, J. et al. TotalSegmentator: robust segmentation of 104
            anatomic structures in CT images. Radiol. Artif. Intell. 5, e230024
            (2023). DOI 10.1148/ryai.230024

AbdomenAtlas 1.0
  Licence : the licence stated at the repository
  Source  : https://github.com/MrGiovanni/AbdomenAtlas
  Role    : abdominal computed tomography volumes and organ labels for pretraining.
  Note    : distributed through the project's own download channels; not
            redistributed here.
  Citation: Li, W. et al. AbdomenAtlas: a large-scale, detailed-annotated,
            multi-center dataset for efficient transfer learning and open
            algorithmic benchmarking. Med. Image Anal. 97, 103285 (2024).

TotalSegmentator reference implementation
  Licence : Apache License 2.0
  Source  : https://github.com/wasserth/TotalSegmentator
  Role    : the reference label set the pretraining manifest names.

Software dependencies
---------------------

NumPy            BSD 3-Clause        https://numpy.org
PyYAML           MIT                 https://pyyaml.org
scikit-learn     BSD 3-Clause        https://scikit-learn.org
PyTorch          BSD 3-Clause        https://pytorch.org

The evaluation in this release uses a release-local implementation of the
DeLong covariance, the intraclass correlation, the chi-square survival function
and the clustered bootstrap; no third-party statistics library is required for
those.

Clinical cohort
---------------

The study cohort of the manuscript is not bundled and no derived record of it is
present in this repository. The release ships a generator that produces a
cohort fixture with the same schema, whose cross-sections are prescribed in
closed form. The generator carries no patient data of any kind.
